Document (dev.stxt.website): Stability and versions | STXT

	Metadata:
		Last modif: 2026-09-16
		Description: STXT is a living language with a stable core. Each specification carries a date and a status (Genesis, Aurora, Zenith or Twilight) instead of a version number; the status defines the level of stability.

	Header: Stability and versions

	Assert >>
		**The syntax of @STXT@ is stable, with no changes planned**.

	Subheader: A living language, with a stable core

	Content >>
		**@STXT@ has evolved**. Today the core is stable and no incompatible changes are expected.
		Schemas and templates are stable too, but an incompatible change is not ruled out.

		For this reason, instead of a numbering, a descriptive system with two variables has been established:

		* **Date** in force: last modification of the document
		* **Status**: indicates the level of stability

		| Status | Level of stability |
		|---|---|
		| **Genesis** | Under construction. Anything may change. |
		| **Aurora** | Usable. Few changes are expected. An incompatible change is announced. |
		| **Zenith** | Stable. There should be no incompatible change. Whatever is added is always compatible with what exists. |
		| **Twilight** | Marked as obsolete, with no changes except errata. |

		The status **only moves forward**, in the order above.

	Subheader: Current status of the specifications

	Content >>
		| Specification | Status | Since |
		|---|---|---|
		| [STXT-SPEC](stxt-core-ref), the base syntax | **Zenith** | 2026-09-07 |
		| [STXT-TREE-SPEC](stxt-tree-ref), the canonical tree and writing | **Zenith** | 2026-09-07 |
		| [STXT-SCHEMA-SPEC](stxt-schema-ref), schemas | **Aurora** | 2026-09-07 |
		| [STXT-TEMPLATE-SPEC](stxt-template-ref), templates | **Aurora** | 2026-09-07 |
		| [STXT-DISCOVERY-SPEC](stxt-discovery-ref), locating definitions | **Aurora** | 2026-09-07 |
